# The point of this journal is its CRLF line endings. Without -text a checkout
# that normalises line endings would hand the test an LF file, and it would
# pass without testing anything.
Tests/SwiftLedgerTests/Conformance/comment-block-crlf.journal -text

# This one mixes CRLF and LF lines on purpose and ends in a lone CR.
Tests/SwiftLedgerTests/Conformance/mixed-line-endings.journal -text

# A carriage return in the middle of a line is the point of this one.
Tests/SwiftLedgerTests/Conformance/amount-stray-cr.journal -text

# CRLF on every line again, this time in a journal with account directives.
Tests/SwiftLedgerTests/Conformance/account-directive-crlf.journal -text

# A carriage return in the middle of an account name is the point of this one.
Tests/SwiftLedgerTests/Conformance/account-directive-stray-cr.journal -text
